$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis via HWE-olefination: To a solution of triethylphosphonoacetate
(1.68 g, 7.50 mmol) in dry and degassed THF (20 mL) was added NaH (300
mg, 7.50 mmol, 60 wt-% dispersion in mineral oil). The mixture was heated
to reflux for 0.5 h and then cooled to 0°C. A solution of 3a (811 mg,
5.00 mmol) in THF (5 mL) was added, and the mixture was heated to reflux
for 1 h, then cooled to ambient temperature and carefully acidified with
HCl (aq., 1 M). The mixture was extracted with MTBE (3 times, 50 mL
each), the combined organic extracts were dried with MgSO4, filtered and
evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column chromatography in
silica using hexane-MTBE mixtures as eluent. 8a (1.02 g, 4.40 mmol, 88%).
Colourless oil. Ethyl (E)-3-(2-(allyloxy)phenyl)acrylate (8a). 4 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.05 (d, J = 16.2 Hz, 1H), 7.51 (dd, J = 7.7, 1.4 Hz,
1H), 7.30 (td, J = 7.9, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 6.94 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.88 (d, J
= 8.3 Hz, 1H), 6.52 (d, J = 16.2 Hz, 1H), 6.07 (ddt, J = 17.2, 10.5, 5.1
Hz, 1H), 5.42 (ddd, J = 17.4, 3.1, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 5.30 (ddd, J = 10.4, 2.5,
1.2 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (dt, J = 5.1, 1.4 Hz, 2H), 4.25 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H),
1.33 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.5, 157.3, 134.0,
133.0, 131.3, 128.8, 123.8, 120.9, 118.8, 117.7, 112.6, 69.2, 60.3, 14.4;
IR (ATR) ν 1705 (s), 1630 (m), 1241 (m), 1160 (s), 749 (s) HRMS (EI)
calcd. for C14H16O3 [M+] 232.1099, found 232.1091.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons reaction, alternative
preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Allyl- and Prenylcoumarins via Microwave-Promoted Tandem
Claisen Rearrangement/Wittig Olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schmidt, Bernd; Riemer, Martin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2016), 48(1), 141-149

