$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a suspension of 0.72 (1.5 mmol) of the
triphenylphosphonium salt, 0.23 g (1.5 mmol) of 4-nitrobenzaldehyde, and
0.32 g (3 mmol) of sodium carbonate in 10 mL of chloroform we added 1.0
mL of water, and the mixture was stirred for 2 h at 25°C. The organic
layer was separated, washed with 5 mL of water, and evaporated. Yield
0.45 g (90%), yellow crystals.
4-Methyl-2-(2-phenylvinyl)-4H-[1,2,4]triazolo-[1,5-a]benzimidazole (12b)
was synthesized in a similar way. Yield 87%, colorless crystals. Mp
149-150°C (from EtOH). 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3), δ, ppm: 3.87 s (3H, CH3),
7.07 d (1H, =CH, J = 15.9 Hz), 7.23-7.40 m (5H, Harom), 7.52-7.60 m (4H,
=CH, H arom), 7.73 d (1H, 8-H, J = 8.1 Hz). Found, %: C 74.46; H 5.21; N
20.13. C17H14N4. Calculated, %: C 74.43; H 5.14; N 20.42.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 4-Substituted 2-chloromethyl[1,2,4]triazolo[1,5-a]benzimidazoles and
their transformations
