$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a screw-capped pressure tube were added 1.0 mL of anhydrous CH2Cl2 and
aldehyde 13 (68.5 mg, 0.25 mmol), followed by the addition of phosphorane
2a (95.4 mg, 0.3 mmol). The tube was sealed and heated to 80 °C until
full consumption of 13 by TLC analysis. Direct column chromatograph
afforded 14 as slightly yellow oil in 85% yield. The isomeric composition
of the product: 91% ee. HPLC analysis (Chiralpak AS-H, i PrOH/hexane =
1/99, 1.0 mL/min, 230 nm; tr (major) = 13.39 min, tr (minor) = 11.55
min). [α]D 25 = +33.5 (c = 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
7.40-7.39 (m, 2H), 7.34-7.32 (m, 2H), 7.25-7.21 (m, 1H), 6.78-6.68 (m,
2H), 6.61-6.57 (m, 1H), 6.35 (dd, J = 15.3, 10.4 Hz, 1H), 6.24 (d, J =
15.8 Hz, 1H), 5.78 (d, J = 15.4 Hz, 1H), 2.28 (s, 3H), 1.52 (s, 3H), 0.16
(s, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 199.09, 152.32, 137.86, 137.09,
133.53, 129.74, 128.73, 128.07, 127.83, 127.43, 126.50, 75.17, 27.47,
27.33, 2.53; IR (ART) ν 3026.2, 2958.9, 1675.1, 1360.0, 1253.3, 1189.4,
1087.4, 987.3, 837.9, 750.0, 690.7 cm-1; MS (EI): 314 (M+, 4), 299 (6),
271 (74), 224 (17), 181 (38), 117 (23), 91 (35), 73 (100); HRMS (EI):
Exact mass calcd for C19H26O2Si: 314.1702; found: 314.1700.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 91% ee, sealed tube used, Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
