$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis via microwave-promoted Wittig reaction: A solution of 3a (126
mg, 0.78 mmol) and 4a (407 mg, 1.17 mmol) in N,N-diethylaniline (4 mL)
was placed in a reaction vessel suited for microwave irradiation. The
vessel was sealed, placed in the microwave reactor and irradiated at
100°C for 1 h. The mixture was cooled to ambient temperature, diluted
with ethyl acetate (50 mL) and washed three times with HCl (aq., 1 M, 30
mL each). The organic layer was separated, dried with MgSO4, filtered and
evaporated. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
using hexane-MTBE-mixtures as eluent. 8a (152 mg, 0.66 mmol, 84%). Ethyl
(E)-3-(2-(allyloxy)phenyl)acrylate (8a). 4 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.05
(d, J = 16.2 Hz, 1H), 7.51 (dd, J = 7.7, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.30 (td, J = 7.9,
1.7 Hz, 1H), 6.94 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.88 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 6.52 (d,
J = 16.2 Hz, 1H), 6.07 (ddt, J = 17.2, 10.5, 5.1 Hz, 1H), 5.42 (ddd, J =
17.4, 3.1, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 5.30 (ddd, J = 10.4, 2.5, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (dt,
J = 5.1, 1.4 Hz, 2H), 4.25 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 1.33 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H);
13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.5, 157.3, 134.0, 133.0, 131.3, 128.8,
123.8, 120.9, 118.8, 117.7, 112.6, 69.2, 60.3, 14.4; IR (ATR) ν 1705 (s),
1630 (m), 1241 (m), 1160 (s), 749 (s) HRMS (EI) calcd. for C14H16O3 [M+]
232.1099, found 232.1091.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, stereoselective, Wittig reaction, alternative
preparation shown, sealed vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Allyl- and Prenylcoumarins via Microwave-Promoted Tandem
Claisen Rearrangement/Wittig Olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schmidt, Bernd; Riemer, Martin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2016), 48(1), 141-149

