$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: To a screw-capped pressure
tube were added anhydrous CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL), aldehyde 3 (0.50 mmol), and
phosphorane 2a (175.0 mg, 0.55 mmol). Then the tube was sealed and heated
to 80 °C until the full consumption of 3 indicated by TLC analysis. The
solvent CH2Cl2 was removed under reduced pressure and then DMF (1.0 mL)
and (R,R)-1 (30.1 mg, 0.05 mmol) were added. The resulting solution was
stirred at -30 °C for half an hour before TMSCN (125 μL, 1.0 mmol) was
charged. After TLC analysis indicated the end of the reaction, the
reaction mixture was poured into NH4Cl (sat.), after usual work-up
procedure and column chromatography using PE/Et2O (10:0 to10:1) as the
eluent could afford the corresponding products 5. The reaction with 3a
was conducted for 12 hours for step 1 and 3 days for step 2; Column
chromatography afforded 5a in 71% yield as colorless oil.26 The reaction
with 3f was conducted for 6 hours for step 1 and 2 days for step 2;
Column chromatography afforded 5f in 84% yield as colorless oil; The
enantiomeric excess of 5f was determined after the acetate 5fa. [α]D 25 =
-2.8 (c = 1.02, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.30-7.27 (m, 2H),
7.21-7.16 (m, 3H), 6.04-5.99 (m, 1H), 5.49-5.45 (m, 1H), 2.64 (t, J = 7.7
Hz, 2H), 2.13-2.09 (m, 2H), 1.79-1.71 (m, 2H), 1.62 (s, 3H), 0.21 (s,
9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 142.00, 132.31, 131.33, 128.49, 128.45,
125.95, 121.09, 69.86, 35.46, 31.32, 30.95, 30.40, 1.52; IR (KBr) ν
3027.5, 2989.7, 2859.1, 1453.8, 1253.9, 1109.8, 1001.8, 971.6, 699.37
cm-1; MS (EI): 287 (M+, 1.1), 260 (18), 182 (21), 169 (74), 104 (100), 91
(61), 75 (68), 53 (36); HRMS (EI): Exact mass calcd for C17H25NOSi:
287.1705, found: 287.1709.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 90% ee(determined after acetate), sealed tube used,
Wittig reaction (stage 1)
