$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of β-sulfenylated acrylates 4. A
25-mL round-bottom flask was charged with thiophenol 1 (0.5 mmol), acetyl
chloride 2a (0.5 mmol), Wittig reagent 3 (0.5 mmol), Cs2CO3 (1.0 mmol),
Et3N (0.5 mmol), CH2Cl2 (2 mL), and DMF (2 mL).The vessel was stirred at
100°C(reflux) in air atmosphere (1 at air balloon) for 10 h. Upon
completion (TLC), the reaction mixture was allowed to cool down to room
temperature and H2O (5 mL) was added. The resulting suspension was
extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 8 mL). The organic phases were combined
and dried over Na2SO4. After filtration and removing the solvent at
reduced pressure, the residue was subjected to silica gel column
chromatography by using 100:1 (v/v) petroleum ether/ethyl acetate as an
eluant to give pure product. Ethyl (E)-3-(p-tolylthio)but-2-enoate (4a).
Colorless liquid. 1H NMR: δ = 7.37 (d, 2H, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.23 (d, 2H, J =
8.0 Hz), 5.21 (s, 1H), 4.07 (q, 2H, J = 7.2 Hz), 2.42 (s, 3H), 2.39 (s,
3H), 1.21 (t, 3H, J = 7.0 Hz); 13C NMR: δ = 165.5, 160.5, 140.2, 135.5,
130.6, 126.0, 110.4, 59.5, 21.4, 20.0, 14.3.HRMS(ESI):m/z [M+Na]+ Calcd.
for C13H16NaO2S: 259.0769; Found: 259.0758.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Wittig reaction, optimization study, optimized on
stoichiometry of reagent, reagent, solvent and temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Three-component reactions of phosphorus ylides, thiophenols, and acetyl
chloride for the synthesis of (β-thioacrylates)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Yunyun; Huang, Bin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Phosphorus, Sulfur and Silicon and the Related Elements (2016), 191(6),
926-929

